==========================================
NETWORKING DAY 06 NOTES — nmap Part 3
Date: 04-10-2026
==========================================

WHAT I LEARNED TODAY:
- -sV actually probes a port and checks the response, instead of just guessing from the port number
- --version-intensity (0-9) trades speed for thoroughness when detecting versions
- -O guesses the operating system based on subtle quirks in how the TCP/IP stack responds - never 100% certain
- -A combines OS detection + version detection + NSE scripts + traceroute into one scan - thorough but slow/noisy
- A stuck scan can be suspended (Ctrl+Z) then properly killed (kill %1) rather than left dangling - lesson from Day 05

COMMANDS I PRACTICED:
[ ] nmap -sV 127.0.0.1 / nmap -sV scanme.nmap.org
[ ] nmap -sV --version-intensity 2 scanme.nmap.org
[ ] sudo nmap -O 127.0.0.1 / sudo nmap -O scanme.nmap.org
[ ] sudo nmap -A -p 22,80 scanme.nmap.org

paste your real output here :
$ nmap -sV scanme.nmap.org
> 

$ sudo nmap -O scanme.nmap.org
> 

$ sudo nmap -A -p 22,80 scanme.nmap.org
> 


